    "share_count_basis": "FY2026 10-K weighted diluted shares 383M (basic 345M + 38M incremental from awards, convertible notes and the converted Series A preferred). Year-end basic was 361M (cover page 360.5M at 2026-08-07) after preferred and partial convertible conversions; the remaining $1,060M convertible principal is classified current and is deep in the money. Principal is kept in net debt (cash settlement of principal) and only the excess conversion value is assumed to sit inside the 383M diluted count. Held FLAT: SBC is fully expensed, and buybacks ($2,592M FY2026, $3.26B authorization remaining) fund the flat count.",
    "wacc_rationale": "USD flows, USD rate: 10-yr UST ~4.3% + beta ~1.3 x 5% ERP = ~10.8% cost of equity; with almost no debt WACC = 10.5%, the house US hardware/tech default. Cyclicality is charged in the scenario flows and the probability weights (bear 30%), not by a WACC premium, and WACC is identical across scenarios (risk charged once).",
    "lease_treatment": "US GAAP ASC 842 operating leases: lease expense ($37M) already sits inside operating costs and EBITDA, so leases are an operating cost (treatment B); the $139M operating lease liability is excluded from net debt. lease_cost_pct_path = 0.",
    "nci_treatment": "No material non-controlling interest.",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF with mid-cycle normalization (routing row: operating company, cyclical; same treatment as BSL.AX, HAL, BAP.AX). WDC is a pure-play HDD maker since the SanDisk spin-off (2025-02-21); pre-FY2025 history consolidates Flash and is not comparable, and CSV FY2023-FY2024 rows are HDD continuing-operations restatements. NORMALIZATION: FY2026 GAAP net income of $9,424M includes a $6,498M unrealized mark-to-market gain on the retained SanDisk stake and a $545M debt-extinguishment loss from the SanDisk-share debt-for-equity exchanges; none of that is in the flows. The model starts from revenue and operating EBITDA (FY2026 GAAP operating income $4,453M + D&A $375M = EBITDA $4,828M, 37.4%; +SBC = 39.0% pre-SBC; Q4 FY2026 exit run-rate ~45.6%). EquitySecuritiesFvNi is $0 at 2026-07-03: the SanDisk stake was fully used in the exchanges, so there is no stake to add in the bridge. Owner FCF FY2026 = reported FCF 3,511 - SBC 204 = 3,307. Interest income ($51M) is NOT stripped because net cash ($527M) is well under 1x the FCF base. FY2026 cash taxes $734M (~17% of operating pre-tax) included a $627M drawdown of accrued taxes; 17% cash tax rate used throughout (Thai/Malaysian tax holidays, FDII, Pillar 2 floor). CYCLE VIEW: FY2027 is still an upcycle year (sold out for calendar 2026, Q4 FY2026 revenue $3.75B annualizes to +16% before further price rises), so year 1 is not cut; the base then assumes the historical HDD pattern reasserts itself in FY2029-FY2030 as Toshiba's capacity doubling and Seagate/WDC HAMR yield gains add exabyte supply, with mid-cycle pre-SBC EBITDA margin of 32% (historical HDD peak was ~25-30% and trough negative; 32% credits duopoly discipline and HAMR). Terminal cap multiples are scenario-specific because the bull thesis IS that the cycle has been structurally damped: 10x bear, 13x base, 16x bull. Working capital is negative capture (manufacturer: receivables + inventory > payables). The Analysis JSON guidance block is the Q3 FY2026 vintage; Q1 FY2027 guidance (issued with Q4 results in August 2026) was not in the research corpus. Replace the year-1 path once it has been read.",
